@ccapndave based on http://stackoverflow.com/a/8216192 this would serve as a recursive check:

``` php
private function getFormErrors($form)
{
    $errors = array();

    if (count($form->all()) > 0) {
        foreach ($form->all() as $child) {
            if (!$child->isValid()) {
                $errors[$child->getName()] = $this->getFormErrors($child);
                if (count($errors[$child->getName()]) === 0) {
                    unset($errors[$child->getName()]);
                }
            }
        }
    } else {
        foreach ($form->getErrors() as $key => $error) {
            $errors[] = $error->getMessage();
        }
    }
    return $errors;
}
```

which would modify your workaround to:

``` php
if ($myForm->isValid() || count($this->getFormErrors($myForm)) === 0) {
    // ok, proceed
}
```

